  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to consider and compare the variances of the lotteries and prefer the one with higher variance (Lottery B). However, the individual in the report focused solely on the probability of winning (i.e., the likelihood of receiving a non-zero amount), which is unrelated to variance. The information considered (probabilities of non-zero outcomes) does not align with the information required by the variance-based reason. Furthermore, the justification (favoring a higher chance of winning) contradicts the variance-based rule: Lottery A has higher probability of a win but lower variance, so choosing A based on 'wahrscheinlicher gewinn' would be inconsistent with the variance preference. Therefore, the individual did not use the variance-based decision reason. The assessment is certain that the reason was not used.",
